validate/linked_dir.jl — running log (2026-11-15). Hypotheses are written before each test.
Criteria: validate/linked_dir_criteria.md (committed before any comparison on the fresh set J).
Development data: D (linked_decay's development set, seeds KSEED + 100j + r) and H′ (linked_ld's
confirmation set, seeds HSEED + 100j + r), re-run with the directional instrumentation (the
instrumentation draws nothing, so these are bitwise the runs of linked_source/linked_ld). Both sets'
association statistics have been seen in earlier studies (disclosed); F and G are not re-run
(budget). The statement that "a mean-skew closure for b κ(B,x,G) failed on D and G" comes from the
task description (a scratch study not in the repository); it was not re-checked here.

== 0. Instrumentation (`dir_run`, `dir_check`) ==

Exact first-order directional changes as derivatives of the statistics under weights 1 + εh,
h = G − Ḡ (individual genotypes), multiplied by β (regression of π/π̄ on G, as the T recursion uses):
  δy_s = E[h e_s d] = κ(B_s, l, G) + (cross-chromosome sampling term, zero in expectation)
  δT_s, δJ_s, δH_s, δK_s (central-moment derivatives, formulas in dir_measure!), δ(y_s Y_l).
Check (QT1000-Possion3.0/Input-09697.txt, 6 generations): V_G bitwise identical to `simulate`; y, T, K,
H, J, yY, K3, TY, JY, yC, yJ equal linked_source's `ls_run`; derivatives equal central finite
differences of `ls_measure!` under weights 1 ± εh (max relative error 3e-9); bin-matrix row sums equal
the group × bin statistics. PASS.

== 1. Size of the directional terms on H′ (72 runs re-made with `dir_run`; kernel CPU not timed (the
   wall clock jumped while the machine slept), estimated ~45 CPU-min from D's 32 CPU-min for 39 runs) ==

Disclosure: the hypotheses for sections 1 and 2 were formulated before the runs but written into this
log only after seeing section 1's output (a lapse; from section 3 on they are written first).
Hypotheses: (i) all three directional terms vanish before the move (symmetry G → −G) and grow after
it; (ii) the T recursion's directional source β(K + K3) equals the measured β δT (identity check);
(iii) the y term is +0.01–0.015 of Σ yY per generation in 0..49 (linked_ld section 1); (iv) the K term
makes K fall in magnitude late in the move (linked_source).

Medians over the 24 H′ inputs of (window mean of the per-generation directional change) / |window
mean of the statistic| (`terms H 3`):
