Reading: (i) holds; (ii) holds (the T recursion's source is the exact directional change); (iii) holds
in 0..24 (+0.013) but the term changes sign by input later: its own-skew part (s_l y_s y_t) is
consistently positive, the partner part (Σ_k s_k D_kl) is positive early and strongly negative in the
5000-locus inputs (−0.07 to −0.25 at 50..99); (iv) holds: K (negative) gains +0.015 to +0.05 of |K|
per generation in 25..99. Per-input values scatter widely (|K| small in some inputs).
Two candidate closures of β Σ δK from the pairwise biallelic model (PBM: two-locus binary joint law
P_kP_l(1 + D d_kd_l/(v_kv_l)), cumulants to second order in D) do NOT reproduce it at the measured
state: the product terms −β(6ΣT_lY_l + 4ΣJ_lY_l) give −0.011/−0.010/−0.002/−0.020 and the
first-order pair term β Σ_l (s_l Σ_k w_k D_kl + w_l Σ_k s_k D_kl) (w = s² − 2v = κ4/v) +0.000/+0.004/
+0.001/+0.014, against the measured −0.004/+0.015/+0.050/−0.015.

