Reading: as hypothesised, the own-skew closure of the y term overpredicts Σ E[yY] once the move has
run (it accumulates without the saturation the kernel shows: measured Σ Q^T stays at 1–3.5e-3 Σ P);
on D it moves H and the 50..99 ΣC toward the kernel, on H′ it overshoots. The K3 closure (BdT) improves
25..49 on H′ but worsens 50..99 there (K3 from the predicted mean LD m, not the measured). Neither
closes the late-move overprediction of ΣC, which section 2 traced to the (unclosed) K term.
Decision (development, disclosed): level B‡ for the pre-specified test on J is Bdag, the closure with
every term this study could derive (own-skew y term, K3, Σκ3 coupling); BdT and B′* are comparators.
The K term and the partner part of the y term are not closed (section 4). Because a closure cannot
test the diagnosis itself, the driven diagnostic (B′* with the measured directional terms and
measured K3/Σκ3: Bdt) is also re-tested on J as a pre-specified secondary claim.

