== pre-specified verdicts (validate/linked_dir_criteria.md, no amendment) ==
Level B‡:
 (a) Σ E[yY] ratio 50..99 1.359, 100..199 3.939 -> FAIL
 (b) Σ H ratio 50..99 1.368 -> FAIL
 (c) Σ K ratio −60..−1 0.966, 50..99 1.176 -> PASS
 (d) ΣC 25..49 +0.023/0.340 ok, 50..99 +0.315/0.498 fails, 100..199 +2.597/2.597 fails, loss +0.433/0.558
     fails -> FAIL
 (e) P1 decay rate: accuracy ok/ok/fails (100..199 +0.334, |lr| 0.334), comparator condition holds -> PARTIAL
Comparators (no verdict, same rules): B′* (a) PASS, (b) FAIL, (c) PARTIAL, (d) FAIL; BdT the same.
Secondary, the diagnosis (B′* + measured directional terms + measured K3/Σκ3, Bdt): ΣC 25..49
−0.060/0.255 ok, 50..99 +0.127/0.290 ok, 100..199 +0.581/0.792 fails, loss +0.192/0.223 ok -> PARTIAL
(Bd, measured directional terms only: PARTIAL, 100..199 +0.788/0.830).

Measured directional terms on J (`terms J 3`, medians per generation ÷ |window mean|, 0..24/25..49/
50..99/100..199): β Σδ(yY)/yY +0.011/+0.015/+0.001/+0.004 (own-skew part +0.002/+0.004/+0.004/+0.006,
partner part +0.005/+0.005/−0.010/−0.008); β ΣδH/|H| +0.004/+0.005/+0.003/+0.022; β ΣδK/|K|
−0.023/−0.014/−0.005/+0.029; β ΣδT vs β Σ(K + K3) equal (identity).

Reading.
 - The diagnosis replicates on fresh inputs for H and K: adding the measured directional terms to B′*
   moves Σ H at 50..99 from 0.45 to 0.93 of measured and Σ K from 1.40 to 0.92 (H′: 0.48 → 0.86,
   1.49 → 0.87); the y term moves Σ E[yY] by +0.08 at 50..99 and lowers its scatter. With the measured
   K3/Σκ3 as well, ΣC passes 25..49, 50..99 and the cumulative loss, but the 100..199 overprediction
   is only reduced (lr +1.44 → +0.58), not removed: the directional terms carry most, not all, of it
   (hypothesis "median within ±0.3 at 100..199" false). Note P1 itself, with the measured K, misses
   at 100..199 on J (+0.33): part of the late gap is in the T recursion's decay or in what drives it,
   not in K.
 - The closure does not. B‡'s own-skew y term grows without the saturation the kernel shows
   (Σ E[yY] 3.9× measured at 100..199, as on development), which inflates H; its K3 closure moves the
   early windows the right way but does not fix 50..99. The K term (the main one) and the partner part
   of the y term are not closed at this order (section 4: the partner part is dominated by three-locus
   third cumulants; the K term is a ~5% residual of a cancellation that needs the cubic heterogeneity
   Cov(B_sB², d_l²) as a state). (c) passes for B‡ only because its inflated H offsets B′*'s K error
   at 50..99 (1.18 vs B′*'s 1.40), not because K is closed: an error cancellation, not a success.
 - P1 is PARTIAL on J (first non-PASS after F, G, H′): the decay rate holds in 25..99, late-window
   accuracy fails narrowly (median lr +0.334 > 0.2).
 - The optional driven-spectrum check was not run ((d) failed, as the task prescribes).

